# The songs themselves are not in git - see drive/CLAUDE.md.
#
# They are other people's recordings; this repo is public and the site is
# public, so the files are put on the box by hand and the manifest beside this
# file is the only part of the music that is version controlled. A slug whose
# file is missing plays nothing and is not an error, so a fresh clone runs.
# **`sfx/` is the exception and it is committed**, because those are not the
# same problem: one short recording under a licence that permits redistribution,
# with its attribution in `sfx/CREDITS.md`. Being in git is the point - it is a
# game sound rather than a soundtrack, so a fresh clone, CI and the deploy all
# have to have it without anybody rsyncing anything.
*
!.gitignore
!music.json
!sfx/
!sfx/**
